  "design_guidance": {
    "observed_issue": "A velocity-named SDK request returns zero status while RL_BALANCE_STAND has a finite pose response. On the captured controller, changing the request to zero changes physical alignment. API names alone cannot justify treating a held nonzero input as stationary intent.",
    "required_identification": "Use the official API and loopback simulator to test bounded per-axis steps, return-to-zero and hold, with actual RobotState and image-derived target error. Estimate input sign, 2x2 image-error response Jacobian, response time, deadband and posture bounds. No scene truth is required.",
    "outer_loop_if_a_posture_hold_regime_is_confirmed": {
      "error": "e = measured laser/target image-derived 2D error; J = measured d(error)/d(official input).",
      "update": "w = -pseudo_inverse(J) @ e; u = saturate(u_trim + Kp*w + I); I += Ki*w*actual_dt for fresh unique valid observations only.",
      "anti_windup": "Freeze/inhibit integral while saturated in the error-driving direction, during blocked mode changes or invalid/stale observations. Rebase or reset after mode changes/target switches rather than replaying an old correction.",
      "settled_hold": "Once aligned, freeze the integral and retain the bounded equilibrium input; verify new frames remain within 8 mm and actual gyro/speed remain under existing limits continuously for 0.4 s. Do not replace a valid held-posture input with zero merely on entry to READY.",
      "safety": "Any stale observation, invalid source feedback, continuing motion, posture limit or unknown control regime revokes firing. A controlled nonzero posture input must remain explicitly distinguishable from nonzero angular velocity."
    },
    "strict_velocity_stop_contract": "If the official/competition contract requires every velocity parameter to equal zero before firing, nonzero hold cannot be relabeled as stop. Send zero, invalidate the old alignment token, acquire post-zero images and establish a fresh stationary dwell. If zero necessarily recenters off target, use a documented official posture-hold interface or adjust neutral pose/position through supported controls; otherwise the chosen API cannot meet that combination of requirements.",
    "avoid": [
      "Do not increase timeout to mask a steady plateau.",
      "Do not relax the 8 mm threshold or fire using a pre-zero image.",
